oggles their action only while held; releasing the key restores the previous state:",["42.25 Momentary Latching Shortcuts"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/25%20Momentary%20Latching%20Shortcuts/","source-block-566","A — Arrangement automation mode",["42.25 Momentary Latching Shortcuts","Holding some shortcut keys for about 500 ms toggles their action only while held; releasing the key restores the previous state:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/25%20Momentary%20Latching%20Shortcuts/","source-block-606","B — Draw Mode",["42.25 Momentary Latching Shortcuts","Holding some shortcut keys for about 500 ms toggles their action only while held; releasing the key restores the previous state:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/25%20Momentary%20Latching%20Shortcuts/","source-block-628","S — solo the selected track",["42.25 Momentary Latching Shortcuts","Holding some shortcut keys for about 500 ms toggles their action only while held; releasing the key restores the previous state:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/25%20Momentary%20Latching%20Shortcuts/","source-block-664","Z — zoom to the Arrangement selection",["42.25 Momentary Latching Shortcuts","Holding some shortcut keys for about 500 ms toggles their action only while held; releasing the key restores the previous state:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/25%20Momentary%20Latching%20Shortcuts/","source-block-710","F1…F8 — Track Activator for the first eight tracks",["42.25 Momentary Latching Shortcuts","Holding some shortcut keys for about 500 ms toggles their action only while held; releasing the key restores the previous state:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/25%20Momentary%20Latching%20Shortcuts/","source-block-773","Tab — Arrangement or Session View",["42.25 Momentary Latching Shortcuts","Holding some shortcut keys for about 500 ms toggles their action only while held; releasing the key restores the previous state:"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/25%20Momentary%20Latching%20Shortcuts/","source-block-815","The Options.txt entry -DisableHotKeyLatching turns latching off.",["42.25 Momentary Latching Shortcuts"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/","source-block-297","42.26 General Keyboard Navigation and Workflow",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/","source-block-459","Most menus, views and controls can be reached from the keyboard. The Navigate menu moves focus between areas of the interface and holds the Tab navigation options; more are in the Display & Input Settings.",["42.26 General Keyboard Navigation and Workflow"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/","source-block-670","Ableton/Live/UG/41 Accessibility and Keyboard Nav/04 Navigating in Live covers each view.",["42.26 General Keyboard Navigation and Workflow"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/01%20Using%20Tab%20for%20Navigation/","source-block-291","42.26.1 Using Tab for Navigation",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/01%20Using%20Tab%20for%20Navigation/","source-block-423","With Use Tab to Move Focus on, Tab / Shift+Tab move to the next or previous control, and Option+Tab / Option+Shift+Tab (Mac), Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab (Win) move along a row in the Session or Arrangement mixer.",["42.26.1 Using Tab for Navigation"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/01%20Using%20Tab%20for%20Navigation/","source-block-650","With it off, Tab switches between Session and Arrangement View.",["42.26.1 Using Tab for Navigation"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/01%20Using%20Tab%20for%20Navigation/","source-block-719","Wrap Tab Navigation — Tab past the last control returns to the first, and Shift+Tab on the first goes to the last.",["42.26.1 Using Tab for Navigation"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/01%20Using%20Tab%20for%20Navigation/","source-block-847","Move Clips with Arrow Keys — on by default; left and right arrows move selected clips or the time selection in the Arrangement. With it off, left and right collapse the time selection to its start or end.",["42.26.1 Using Tab for Navigation"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/01%20Using%20Tab%20for%20Navigation/","source-block-1061","Same content as Ableton/Live/UG/41 Accessibility and Keyboard Nav/01 Menu and Keyboard Navigation Settings/01 Using Tab for Navigation.",["42.26.1 Using Tab for Navigation"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/02%20Navigating%20Between%20Controls%20in%20the%20Settings%20Menu/","source-block-267","42.26.2 Navigating Between Controls in the Settings Menu",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/02%20Navigating%20Between%20Controls%20in%20the%20Settings%20Menu/","source-block-447","Tab and Shift+Tab move between options in a Settings tab, whether or not Use Tab to Move Focus is on. Up and down arrows change a focused option; Enter flips a toggle.",["42.26.2 Navigating Between Controls in the Settings Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/26%20General%20Keyboard%20Navigation%20and%20Workflow/02%20Navigating%20Between%20Controls%20in%20the%20Settings%20Menu/","source-block-624","Option+Tab / Option+Shift+Tab (Mac), Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab (Win), or the arrows on the focused Settings Page Chooser switch tabs. Shift+Tab from a tab's first control returns to the chooser.",["42.26.2 Navigating Between Controls in the Settings Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/27%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes%20with%20the%20Keyboard/","source-block-263","42.27 Editing Automation and Modulation Envelopes with the Keyboard",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/27%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes%20with%20the%20Keyboard/","source-block-467","Breakpoints in automation and modulation envelopes can be added, edited and deleted from the keyboard; see Ableton/Live/UG/41 Accessibility and Keyboard Nav/05 Editing Automation and Modulation Envelopes.",["42.27 Editing Automation and Modulation Envelopes with the Keyboard"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/28%20Accessing%20Menus/","source-block-294","42.28 Accessing Menus",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/28%20Accessing%20Menus/","source-block-406","Mac: Cmd+? opens a search field that suggests menu entries as you type; arrows choose and Enter runs.",["42.28 Accessing Menus"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/28%20Accessing%20Menus/","source-block-515","Windows: Alt plus a menu's first letter opens it, such as Alt+F for File. Up and down move through items, left and right open neighboring menus, and Enter chooses.",["42.28 Accessing Menus"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/29%20Using%20Live%27s%20Context%20Menu/","source-block-170","42.29 Using Live’s Context Menu",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/29%20Using%20Live%27s%20Context%20Menu/","source-block-303","Right-click (Win) or Ctrl-click (Mac) an area of Live for its context menu. From the keyboard: VO+Shift+M (Mac), or Menu or Shift+F10 (Win).",["42.29 Using Live’s Context Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/29%20Using%20Live%27s%20Context%20Menu/","source-block-455","Some context menus include options from Live's Settings; changing them affects the whole program, not just the selected item.",["42.29 Using Live’s Context Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/29%20Using%20Live%27s%20Context%20Menu/","source-block-584","Some commands appear only in context menus, including browser options, grid marker commands for Auto-Warp, grid line width options, copy and paste of Operator envelopes and oscillators, and many device-specific commands.",["42.29 Using Live’s Context Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/43%20Credits/","source-block-130","43. Credits",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/43%20Credits/","source-block-200","The people who wrote the manual and built Live.",["43. Credits"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/","source-block-65","Ableton Live interface",[]],["Ableton/Live/UI/","source-block-92","The views, bars and controls of .",["Ableton Live interface"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/","source-block-145","Areas",["Ableton Live interface"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/","source-block-157","Ableton/Live/UI/Control Bar",["Ableton Live interface","Areas"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/","source-block-193","Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement View",["Ableton Live interface","Areas"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/","source-block-234","Source",["Ableton Live interface"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/","source-block-247","Ableton/Live/UG · Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual",["Ableton Live interface","Source"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement%20View/","source-block-173","Arrangement View",[]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement%20View/","source-block-194","Live's view for arranging a song on a linear timeline, as opposed to the Session View's clip launching.",["Arrangement View"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement%20View/","source-block-301","Areas",["Arrangement View"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement%20View/","source-block-404","Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement View/Scrub Area",["Arrangement View","Areas"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement%20View/","source-block-456","— called the track's main lane in Live 12",["Arrangement View","Areas"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement%20View/","source-block-552","Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement View/Time Ruler",["Arrangement View","Areas"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement%20View/","source-block-604",